# Chairforce Helper Functions Rules

## ⚠️ **Important: Working with Helper Functions**

**Before creating a new helper function:**
1. **Check if it already exists** in `/includes/helper-functions.php`
2. **Avoid shortcuts** - don't modify existing functions unless you're certain about all implications
3. **Create new functions** in the helper functions file when needed
4. **Test thoroughly** - helper functions are used throughout the theme

**File Location**: `/includes/helper-functions.php`

## Build System Helpers
```php
// Get build file URLs & paths
$css_url = chairforce_get_build_url('style.css');
$js_path = chairforce_get_build_dir('script.js');
```

## Media & Image Helpers
```php
// Post thumbnail MIME type & CPT placeholders
$mime_type = chairforce_get_post_thumbnail_mime_type(get_the_ID());
$placeholder = chairforce_get_placeholder_thumbnail_for_cpt('chairforce_faq');

// SVG image handling
$svg_content = chairforce_maybe_get_svg_img($attachment_id);
```

## Block System Helpers
```php
// ACF block CSS classes & taxonomy terms with Yoast
$block_classes = chairforce_get_acf_block_classname($block, 'my-block');
$primary_category = chairforce_get_taxonomy_terms_for_post('category');
```

## Programmatic Buttons in PHP

When PHP code needs to output theme-styled buttons (Load More, header CTAs,
dynamic system UI, etc.), **always use `chairforce_get_buttons_markup()`** in
`/includes/helper-functions.php` — do **not** hand-roll
`<div class="wp-block-button">` / `<a class="wp-block-button__link">` markup.

The helper builds real `core/buttons` + `core/button` block comments and renders
them via `do_blocks()`, so output matches the Site Editor: block styles
(`is-style-primary`, `is-style-ghost`, etc.), layout classes
(`is-layout-flex`, `is-content-justification-center`, `wp-container-core-buttons-*`),
and Lucide icon classes (`cf-has-icon`, `cf-icon-{slug}`).

### When to use

- **Use** for dynamic/system UI authored in PHP classes (`Load_More`, header
  fragments, REST-driven shells, etc.).
- **Do not use** for content CTAs in patterns/templates — those stay normal
  editor blocks.
- **Avoid** calling it in tight loops (e.g. per card in a grid); `do_blocks()`
  has a per-call cost.

### Example — link with Ghost style + Lucide icon

```php
echo chairforce_get_buttons_markup(
    [
        [
            'label' => __( 'Shop now', 'chairforce' ),
            'url'   => home_url( '/shop/' ),
            'style' => 'is-style-ghost',
            'icon'  => 'shopping-cart',
        ],
    ],
    [
        'layout' => [
            'type'           => 'flex',
            'justifyContent' => 'center',
        ],
    ]
);
```

### Example — `<button>` for JS-driven actions (Load More)

```php
echo chairforce_get_buttons_markup(
    [
        [
            'label'           => __( 'Load More', 'chairforce' ),
            'style'           => 'is-style-ghost',
            'element_class'   => 'cf-load-more__button',
            'tag'             => 'button',
            'html_attributes' => [
                'data-next-page' => '2',
                'aria-busy'      => 'false',
            ],
        ],
    ],
    [
        'layout' => [
            'type'           => 'flex',
            'justifyContent' => 'center',
        ],
    ]
);
```

### Button config keys

| Key | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `label` | Button text (required) |
| `url` | Required when `tag` is `a` (default) |
| `tag` | `a` or `button` (maps to core/button `tagName`) |
| `style` | Block style class, e.g. `is-style-ghost` |
| `class` | Extra classes on `.wp-block-button` wrapper |
| `element_class` | Extra classes on the `<a>` / `<button>` element |
| `icon` | Lucide slug → `cf-has-icon` / `cf-icon-{slug}` on wrapper |
| `icon_position` | `left` (default) or `right` |
| `html_attributes` | Extra attrs on the element (`data-*`, `aria-*`, etc.) |
| `external` | Opens link in new tab |

**Args:** `wrapper_class`, `default_style` (default `is-style-primary`), `default_icon`, `layout` (flex/center JSON for `core/buttons`).

**Reference implementation:** `lib/class-load-more.php`.

**Related:** [Icon System](16-icon-system.mdc) — Lucide on buttons (editor vs PHP vs Sass mixins).

